{"id":"mahabharata-3-286","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":286,"title":"षडशीत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 286 · The Sun's counsel: ask for the spear","summary":{"en":"Karna, devoted to the Sun, still refuses to break his vow of giving. The Sun then tells him that if he must give the earrings, he should ask Indra in return for his unfailing spear, and Karna resolves to do so.","kn":"ಸೂರ್ಯಭಕ್ತನಾದ ಕರ್ಣನು ತನ್ನ ದಾನವ್ರತ ಮುರಿಯಲು ಈಗಲೂ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕುಂಡಲ ಕೊಡಲೇಬೇಕಾದರೆ ಪ್ರತಿಯಾಗಿ ಇಂದ್ರನಿಂದ ಅಮೋಘ ಶಕ್ತ್ಯಾಯುಧವನ್ನು ಕೇಳು ಎಂದು ಸೂರ್ಯನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಕರ್ಣನು ಹಾಗೆ ಮಾಡಲು ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सूर्य का भक्त कर्ण फिर भी दान का व्रत तोड़ने से मना करता है। तब सूर्य कहते हैं कि यदि कुण्डल देने ही हैं तो बदले में इन्द्र से उनकी अमोघ शक्ति माँगे, और कर्ण ऐसा करने का निश्चय करता है।","te":"సూర్యభక్తుడైన కర్ణుడు ఇప్పటికీ తన దానవ్రతాన్ని భంగపరచడానికి నిరాకరిస్తాడు. కుండలాలు ఇవ్వక తప్పకపోతే బదులుగా ఇంద్రుని నుండి అమోఘమైన శక్తిని కోరమని సూర్యుడు చెబుతాడు, కర్ణుడు అలా చేయాలని నిశ్చయిస్తాడు.","ta":"சூரிய பக்தனான கர்ணன் இப்போதும் தன் கொடை விரதத்தை மீற மறுக்கிறான். குண்டலங்களைக் கொடுத்தே ஆக வேண்டுமென்றால் பதிலாக இந்திரனிடம் அவனுடைய தவறாத சக்தி ஆயுதத்தைக் கேள் என்று சூரியன் சொல்ல, கர்ணன் அவ்வாறே செய்யத் தீர்மானிக்கிறான்.","ml":"സൂര്യഭക്തനായ കർണ്ണൻ, ദാനവ്രതം ലംഘിക്കാൻ ഇപ്പോഴും വിസമ്മതിക്കുന്നു. കുണ്ഡലങ്ങൾ നൽകണമെങ്കിൽ, പിഴയ്ക്കാത്ത കുന്തം പകരമായി ഇന്ദ്രനോട് ചോദിക്കണമെന്ന് സൂര്യൻ ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു; കർണ്ണൻ അങ്ങനെ ചെയ്യാൻ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.286; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कुण्डलाहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Kundalaharana Parva (Taking of the earrings)","verses":[{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भगवन्तमहं भक्तो यथा मां वेत्थ गोपते ।\nतथा परमतिग्मांशो नान्यं देवं कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of rays, as you know how devoted I am to you, so I am to no other god in any way, you of fierce rays."}},{"n":2,"text":"न मे दारा न मे पुत्रा न चात्मा सुहृदो न च ।\nतथेष्टा वै सदा भक्त्या यथा त्वं गोपते मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither wives nor sons nor myself nor friends are as dear to me, with devotion always, as you are, lord of light."}},{"n":3,"text":"इष्टानां च महात्मानो भक्तानां च न संशयः ।\nकुर्वन्ति भक्तिमिष्टां च जानीषे त्वं च भास्कर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great beings, without doubt, show their dear affection to those who are dear and devoted; and you know it, Bhaskara."}},{"n":4,"text":"इष्टो भक्तश्च मे कर्णो न चान्यद्दैवतं दिवि ।\nजानीत इति वै कृत्वा भगवानाह मद्धितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna is dear and devoted to you, and I have no other god in heaven; knowing this, the lord has spoken for my good."}},{"n":5,"text":"भूयश्च शिरसा याचे प्रसाद्य च पुनः पुनः ।\nइति ब्रवीमि तिग्मांशो त्वं तु मे क्षन्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again and again I bow my head and plead with you, hot-rayed one; please forgive me for what I say."}},{"n":6,"text":"बिभेमि न तथा मृत्योर्यथा बिभ्येऽनृतादहम् ।\nविशेषेण द्विजातीनां सर्वेषां सर्वदा सताम् ।\nप्रदाने जीवितस्यापि न मेऽत्रास्ति विचारणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I fear death not so much as I fear falsehood. Especially in giving to brahmins and all good people, I have no hesitation even if it means my life."}},{"n":7,"text":"यच्च मामात्थ देव त्वं पाण्डवं फल्गुनं प्रति ।\nव्येतु संतापजं दुःखं तव भास्कर मानसम् ।\nअर्जुनं प्रति मां चैव विजेष्यामि रणेऽर्जुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As for what you said, god, about Phalguna the Pandava, let the distress born of worry leave your heart, Bhaskara. I will conquer Arjuna in battle."}},{"n":8,"text":"तवापि विदितं देव ममाप्यस्त्रबलं महत् ।\nजामदग्न्यादुपात्तं यत्तथा द्रोणान्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know too, god, that I have great power with weapons, obtained from Jamadagni's son and from great Drona."}},{"n":9,"text":"इदं त्वमनुजानीहि सुरश्रेष्ठ व्रतं मम ।\nभिक्षते वज्रिणे दद्यामपि जीवितमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Please permit me this vow, best of gods: if the wielder of the thunderbolt begs, I would give even my own life."}},{"text":"सूर्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surya said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"यदि तात ददास्येते वज्रिणे कुण्डले शुभे ।\nत्वमप्येनमथो ब्रूया विजयार्थं महाबल ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you give these fine earrings to the wielder of the thunderbolt, dear son, then you should say this to him, mighty one, for victory."}},{"n":11,"text":"नियमेन प्रदद्यास्त्वं कुण्डले वै शतक्रतोः ।\nअवध्यो ह्यसि भूतानां कुण्डलाभ्यां समन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should give the earrings to Indra, of a hundred sacrifices, on a condition, for with these earrings you cannot be killed by any being."}},{"n":12,"text":"अर्जुनेन विनाशं हि तव दानवसूदनः ।\nप्रार्थयानो रणे वत्स कुण्डले ते जिहीर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The slayer of the Danavas wants your earrings, child, seeking your destruction at Arjuna's hand in battle."}},{"n":13,"text":"स त्वमप्येनमाराध्य सूनृताभिः पुनः पुनः ।\nअभ्यर्थयेथा देवेशममोघार्थं पुरंदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore you too, propitiating him again and again with pleasant words, should ask Indra, lord of gods, whose purposes never fail:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अमोघां देहि मे शक्तिममित्रविनिबर्हिणीम् ।\nदास्यामि ते सहस्राक्ष कुण्डले वर्म चोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give me your unfailing spear that destroys enemies; then, thousand-eyed one, I will give you the earrings and the excellent armor."}},{"n":15,"text":"इत्येवं नियमेन त्वं दद्याः शक्राय कुण्डले ।\nतया त्वं कर्ण संग्रामे हनिष्यसि रणे रिपून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Only on this condition should you give the earrings to Indra; with that spear, Karna, you will kill your enemies in battle."}},{"n":16,"text":"नाहत्वा हि महाबाहो शत्रूनेति करं पुनः ।\nसा शक्तिर्देवराजस्य शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For that spear of the king of the gods, mighty-armed one, does not return to the hand without slaying enemies, hundreds and thousands of them."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा सहस्रांशुः सहसान्तरधीयत ।\nततः सूर्याय जप्यान्ते कर्णः स्वप्नं न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the thousand-rayed one suddenly vanished. Then at the end of his prayers Karna told Surya about the dream."}},{"n":18,"text":"यथादृष्टं यथातत्त्वं यथोक्तमुभयोर्निशि ।\nतत्सर्वमानुपूर्व्येण शशंसास्मै वृषस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, the Vrisha, then told him in order all that he had seen and what had been said by both in the night, just as it was."}},{"n":19,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा भगवान्देवो भानुः स्वर्भानुसूदनः ।\nउवाच तं तथेत्येव कर्णं सूर्यः स्मयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing it, the divine lord Surya, slayer of Svarbhanu, said to Karna, smiling as it were, So it is."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततस्तत्त्वमिति ज्ञात्वा राधेयः परवीरहा ।\nशक्तिमेवाभिकाङ्क्षन्वै वासवं प्रत्यपालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, knowing it to be true, Radha's son, destroyer of enemy heroes, waited for Indra, longing only for the spear."}}]}]}